  "notes": "Block 13 cause code 'C' (Design/Manufacturing/Construction/Installation per NRC coding, but the narrative attributes cause to external severe weather; per rule 4, cause_code and category copied verbatim from FORM-366 fields, category left as 'provisional' since FORM-366 stated category is 'provisional'). Two distinct consequences identified: the LOOP/scram event and the separately-discovered Secondary Containment inoperability from storm-damaged wall, both traced back to the same root storm damage. No corrective actions beyond repair were identified since the event was deemed within design basis; ca_repair captures the stated repair/recovery efforts. Previous occurrences are reactor scrams from unrelated causes (feedwater) but are the licensee's own stated 'previous similar occurrences' review, so captured as SIMILAR_TO stubs despite different root causes, per licensee's explicit inclusion."
